CloudBurrow patch 85 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1662).

The emulator keeps its tables, and the results of its jobs (patch 0002),
in a temporary SQLite file (server.TempStorage), which never shrank:
SQLite reuses the pages a DROP TABLE or a dropped result frees, but in its
default auto_vacuum mode, NONE, never gives them back to the filesystem.
Measured in TestBigQueryInformationSchemaJobs -count=200 after the
BigQuery compat suite and 6,000 more jobs (arm64, Docker Desktop): the
file reached 1.01 GB in 23 minutes, on the container's writable layer, so
on the node's disk.

The file is now opened with auto_vacuum=FULL, which a new file takes
before its first table, so each commit truncates the pages it freed; the
file holds what the emulator keeps, not the most it ever kept. Setting a
PRAGMA through the SQLite driver's DSN (_pragma) drops the busy timeout of
one minute the driver sets when none is given, so that one is named
first, as the driver orders them. cloudburrow_auto_vacuum_test.go fails
without the patch (auto_vacuum 0) and passes with it: a 4 MB table's DROP
shrinks the file. Independent of the other patches.

